## Alerts and Dashboard Widgets

Any metric query you build in Explore can become a [Monitor](/product/monitors-and-alerts/monitors/) so you get notified when behavior changes. **Application Metrics** is available as a dataset in the Monitor form (alongside Errors, Spans, Logs, and Releases), with a dedicated template to get started quickly.

Monitors can detect threshold breaches, percentage changes, or dynamic anomalies — then create an issue you route through [Alerts](/product/monitors-and-alerts/alerts/) to Slack, PagerDuty, email, and more.

Once you're bringing in metrics, learn how to [Build a dashboard and alert from custom metrics](https://sentry.io/cookbook/custom-metrics-dashboard-alerts-nextjs/) (~20 min recipe).

You can also add metric visualizations to [Dashboards](/product/dashboards/) and save common Explore queries for quick access.

You can also [create dashboards with an AI coding agent](https://sentry.io/cookbook/create-dashboards-with-ai-agent/) (~15 min recipe).

## Quick Reference

| Category             | Type         | Method           | Example Attributes                        |
| -------------------- | ------------ | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| Business events      | Counter      | `count()`        | user_tier, payment_method, failure_reason |
| Application health   | Counter      | `count()`        | email_type, provider, job_type, queue     |
| Resource utilization | Gauge        | `gauge()`        | queue_name, pool_name                     |
| Latency/performance  | Distribution | `distribution()` | endpoint, method, table, operation        |
| Business values      | Distribution | `distribution()` | user_tier, region, file_type              |

## When to Use Metrics vs Traces vs Logs

| Signal      | Best For                              | Example Question                         |
| ----------- | ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| **Metrics** | Aggregated counts, rates, percentiles | "How many checkouts failed this hour?"   |
| **Traces**  | Request flow, latency breakdown       | "Why was this specific request slow?"    |
| **Logs**    | Detailed context, debugging           | "What happened right before this error?" |

All three are trace-connected. Start wherever makes sense and navigate to the others.

Explore the [Application Metrics product walkthrough](/product/metrics/) to learn more about the Sentry interface and discover additional tips.

