<SdkOption name="onCrashedLastRun" type="function">

**Deprecated.** Use <PlatformIdentifier name="onLastRunStatusDetermined" /> instead, which is called regardless of whether the app crashed.

A block called after SDK initialization when the last execution terminated with a crash. This callback is invoked synchronously during SDK initialization, so keep any work here minimal. It is only executed once during the entire run of the program. Crash reporting is automatically disabled if a debugger is attached, and there is no guarantee this callback runs on the main thread.

```swift {tabTitle:Swift}
import Sentry

SentrySDK.start { options in
    options.dsn = "___PUBLIC_DSN___"
    options.onCrashedLastRun = { _ in
        // Perform actions when a crash was detected on last run
        print("App crashed on last run")
    }
}
```

```objc {tabTitle:Objective-C}
@import Sentry;

[SentrySDK startWithConfigureOptions:^(SentryOptions *options) {
    options.dsn = @"___PUBLIC_DSN___";
    options.onCrashedLastRun = ^(SentryEvent * _Nonnull event) {
        // Perform actions when a crash was detected on last run
        NSLog(@"App crashed on last run");
    };
}];
```

```objc {tabTitle:Objective-C (SentryObjC)}
#import <SentryObjC/SentryObjC.h>

[SentryObjCSDK startWithConfigureOptions:^(SentryObjCOptions *options) {
    options.dsn = @"___PUBLIC_DSN___";
    options.onCrashedLastRun = ^(SentryObjCEvent * _Nonnull event) {
        // Perform actions when a crash was detected on last run
        NSLog(@"App crashed on last run");
    };
}];
```

</SdkOption>

<SdkOption name="onLastRunStatusDetermined" type="function">

A block called shortly after SDK initialization when the crash status of the last program execution has been determined. Unlike <PlatformIdentifier name="onCrashedLastRun" />, this callback is invoked regardless of whether the app crashed:

- If the last run ended with a crash, `status` is `SentryLastRunStatus.didCrash` and `crashEvent` contains the crash event.
- If the last run did not end with a crash, `status` is `SentryLastRunStatus.didNotCrash` and `crashEvent` is `nil`.

This callback is only executed once per `SentrySDK.start(configureOptions:)` lifecycle, and it is not guaranteed to be called on the main thread. Crash reporting is automatically disabled while a debugger is attached, in which case the callback reports `didNotCrash` even if the app crashed.

```swift {tabTitle:Swift}
import Sentry

SentrySDK.start { options in
    options.dsn = "___PUBLIC_DSN___"
    options.onLastRunStatusDetermined = { status, crashEvent in
        switch status {
        case .didCrash:
            print("App crashed on last run: \(String(describing: crashEvent))")
        case .didNotCrash:
            print("App did not crash on last run")
        @unknown default:
            break
        }
    }
}
```

```objc {tabTitle:Objective-C}
@import Sentry;

[SentrySDK startWithConfigureOptions:^(SentryOptions *options) {
    options.dsn = @"___PUBLIC_DSN___";
    options.onLastRunStatusDetermined = ^(SentryLastRunStatus status, SentryEvent * _Nullable crashEvent) {
        if (status == SentryLastRunStatusDidCrash) {
            NSLog(@"App crashed on last run: %@", crashEvent);
        } else {
            NSLog(@"App did not crash on last run");
        }
    };
}];
```

```objc {tabTitle:Objective-C (SentryObjC)}
#import <SentryObjC/SentryObjC.h>

[SentryObjCSDK startWithConfigureOptions:^(SentryObjCOptions *options) {
    options.dsn = @"___PUBLIC_DSN___";
    options.onLastRunStatusDetermined = ^(SentryObjCLastRunStatus status, SentryObjCEvent * _Nullable crashEvent) {
        if (status == SentryObjCLastRunStatusDidCrash) {
            NSLog(@"App crashed on last run: %@", crashEvent);
        } else {
            NSLog(@"App did not crash on last run");
        }
    };
}];
```

</SdkOption>

## Tracing Options

<SdkOption name="tracesSampleRate" type="float">

A number between `0` and `1`, controlling the percentage chance a given transaction will be sent to Sentry. (`0` represents 0% while `1` represents 100%.) Applies equally to all transactions created in the app. Either this or <PlatformIdentifier name="tracesSampler" /> must be defined to enable tracing.

</SdkOption>

<SdkOption name="tracesSampler" type="function">

A function responsible for determining the percentage chance a given transaction will be sent to Sentry. It will automatically be passed information about the transaction and the context in which it's being created, and must return a number between `0` (0% chance of being sent) and `1` (100% chance of being sent). Can also be used for filtering transactions, by returning 0 for those that are unwanted. Either this or <PlatformIdentifier name="tracesSampleRate" /> must be defined to enable tracing.

</SdkOption>

<SdkOption name="tracePropagationTargets" type="array">

An optional property that controls which downstream services receive tracing data, in the form of a `sentry-trace` and a `baggage` header attached to any outgoing HTTP requests.

The option may contain a list of strings or regex against which the URLs of outgoing requests are matched.
If one of the entries in the list matches the URL of an outgoing request, trace data will be attached to that request.
String entries do not have to be full matches, meaning the URL of a request is matched when it _contains_ a string provided through the option.

If <PlatformIdentifier name="tracePropagationTargets" /> is not provided, trace data is attached to every outgoing request from the instrumented client.

</SdkOption>

<SdkOption name="strictTraceContinuation" type="Bool" defaultValue="false">

If set to `true`, the SDK will only continue a trace if the organization ID of the incoming trace found in the `baggage` header matches the organization ID of the current Sentry client.

The client's organization ID is extracted from the DSN or can be set with the `orgId` option.

