## Step 4: Verify Your Setup

Let's test your setup and confirm that Sentry is working correctly and sending data to your Sentry project.

### Issues

<SplitLayout>
<SplitSection>
<SplitSectionText>

Let's verify that Sentry captures errors and creates issues in your Sentry project. Add an intentional error in your function:

</SplitSectionText>
<SplitSectionCode>

```javascript {tabTitle:async}
const Sentry = require("@sentry/node");

module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  try {
    // This function does not exist, triggering an error
    await notExistFunction();
  } catch (e) {
    Sentry.withScope((scope) => {
      scope.setSDKProcessingMetadata({ request: req });
      Sentry.captureException(e);
    });
  }

  // Wait for the event to be sent before the function execution ends
  await Sentry.flush(2000);

  context.res = {
    status: 500,
    body: "Test error sent to Sentry.",
  };
};
```

